      "message": "Hi Evie — in case \"How\" is asking how the kernel-doc was lost:\n\nUpstream commit d5e79eeba308 (\"dma-buf: heaps: Deduplicate docs and adopt common format\") added the colons kernel-doc needs on @heap_devt, @list and @heap_cdev. That hunk never reached android-mainline: merge da0c10aefaf6 resolved this block by taking the new @priv: line from mainline while keeping the android side\u0027s colonless @heap_devt / @list / @heap_cdev, next to the ANDROID-only @heap_dev.\n\nThe original change (4200863) restores the upstream wording, gives @heap_dev the same treatment, and documents @refcount, which was added later with the heap device lifetime handling and never described. scripts/kernel-doc -none drivers/dma-buf/dma-heap.c reports five warnings before it and none after. No functional change, and drm-misc-next is clean here so there is nothing to send upstream.\n\nHappy to clarify if you meant something else.",
